585
00:30:01,880 --> 00:30:04,000
They're designed to start a fire, and more importantly,

586
00:30:04,100 --> 00:30:06,680
to start a fire that turns into a much bigger fire.

587
00:30:06,780 --> 00:30:10,020
The Allies used it in the final phases of World War II

588
00:30:10,120 --> 00:30:11,920
in an effort to hasten the war's end.

589
00:30:15,020 --> 00:30:20,220
The World War II incendiary bomb

590
00:30:20,320 --> 00:30:23,020
resembled a long stick filled with fuel,

591
00:30:23,120 --> 00:30:26,260
weighted down at one end to make it more accurate.

592
00:30:26,360 --> 00:30:29,360
The bomb was either dropped as a single projectile

593
00:30:29,460 --> 00:30:33,280
or packed inside a casing that would break apart before impact,

594
00:30:33,380 --> 00:30:37,280
dispersing hundreds of incendiary sticks in a cluster.

595
00:30:37,380 --> 00:30:40,620
On impact, a heat-producing chemical

596
00:30:40,720 --> 00:30:45,020
activated the incendiary fuel.

597
00:30:45,021 --> 00:30:49,620
On February 13, 1945, British bombers attacked Dresden,

598
00:30:49,720 --> 00:30:53,160
Germany with 300 tons of thermite incendiaries.

599
00:30:53,260 --> 00:30:55,360
Temperatures in the resulting firestorm

600
00:30:55,460 --> 00:30:59,460
reached a staggering 2,700 degrees Fahrenheit.

601
00:30:59,560 --> 00:31:03,100
That fire thrusts up a fountain column

602
00:31:03,200 --> 00:31:06,240
of incandescent gases and burning debris, which

603
00:31:06,340 --> 00:31:07,340
spread the fire.

604
00:31:07,440 --> 00:31:08,880
But more importantly, it acts like a bellows.

605
00:31:08,980 --> 00:31:11,540
It sucks in air and oxygen into the fire

606
00:31:11,640 --> 00:31:15,020
at winds of gale force, which, for example,

607
00:31:15,021 --> 00:31:18,360
will suck individuals back into the fire.

608
00:31:18,460 --> 00:31:20,820
Less than a month after the devastating attack

609
00:31:20,920 --> 00:31:25,240
on Dresden, the US was preparing its own firebombing campaign

610
00:31:25,340 --> 00:31:30,440
against Japan using a new incendiary fuel called napalm.

611
00:31:34,380 --> 00:31:39,280
They came up with a compound of naphthenic and palminic acids,

612
00:31:39,380 --> 00:31:42,480
which were contracted to be called napalm, which

613
00:31:42,481 --> 00:31:44,480
It was mixed with gasoline and produced

614
00:31:44,580 --> 00:31:47,620
by far the most effective incendiary device of World War II.

615
00:31:47,720 --> 00:31:50,320
Napalm burns with extreme intensity,

616
00:31:50,420 --> 00:31:52,660
and its stringy and sticky consistency

617
00:31:52,760 --> 00:31:54,420
allows it to spread more effectively

618
00:31:54,520 --> 00:31:56,860
than other incendiaries.

619
00:31:56,960 --> 00:32:01,000
Incendiary bombs fell on Tokyo on March 9, 1945.

620
00:32:05,980 --> 00:32:08,380
The night raid against Tokyo

621
00:32:08,480 --> 00:32:11,680
was the most devastating single raid ever carried out

622
00:32:11,681 --> 00:32:16,220
by aircraft in any war to include the nuclear bombings

623
00:32:16,320 --> 00:32:19,020
of Hiroshima and Nagasaki.

624
00:32:19,120 --> 00:32:21,720
For it's never before seen destructive power,

625
00:32:21,820 --> 00:32:25,200
both reviled and admired, the incendiary bomb

626
00:32:25,300 --> 00:32:27,320
comes in at number three on our countdown.

627
00:32:32,040 --> 00:32:34,840
As we've counted down our top 10 weapons,

628
00:32:34,940 --> 00:32:38,180
you've witnessed some of the most powerful defense tools,

629
00:32:38,280 --> 00:32:39,900
old and new.

630
00:32:39,901 --> 00:32:44,140
We're nearly ready to unveil number one.

631
00:32:44,240 --> 00:32:46,600
Following the deadly tomahawk at number four

632
00:32:46,700 --> 00:32:49,980
and the terrifying incendiary bomb at number three,

633
00:32:50,080 --> 00:32:53,620
our runner-up at number two, the rapid-fire marvel that

634
00:32:53,720 --> 00:32:59,320
rewrote war's tactical playbook, the Maxim machine gun.

635
00:32:59,420 --> 00:33:01,760
The Maxim machine gun was the world's first completely

636
00:33:01,860 --> 00:33:07,900
automatic weapon, a killing machine unlike any before.

637
00:33:07,901 --> 00:33:10,940
A machine gun could wipe out an entire group of men

638
00:33:11,040 --> 00:33:14,300
very quickly, thousands and thousands of men

639
00:33:14,400 --> 00:33:16,400
in a very short time.

640
00:33:16,500 --> 00:33:19,840
The man behind the weapon was inventor Hiram Maxim,

641
00:33:19,940 --> 00:33:24,580
whose first patent had been for an improved curling iron.

642
00:33:24,680 --> 00:33:27,660
He was a man with a very fertile mind.

643
00:33:27,760 --> 00:33:30,660
And in 1881, he went to London.

644
00:33:30,760 --> 00:33:35,100
While there, one of his friends reportedly said to him,

645
00:33:35,101 --> 00:33:38,940
Hiram, why don't you develop a new way for Europeans

646
00:33:38,941 --> 00:33:40,040
to kill each other?

647
00:33:40,160 --> 00:33:41,500
They're always at each other's throats.

648
00:33:41,560 --> 00:33:42,600
You can make a lot of money.

649
00:33:43,440 --> 00:33:44,600
He kind of said, oh, OK.

650
00:33:45,160 --> 00:33:46,400
I'll invent some guns.

651
00:33:47,380 --> 00:33:52,580
And within a couple of years, I mean, it took that little time.

652
00:33:53,000 --> 00:33:54,460
He had invented the machine gun.

653
00:33:54,920 --> 00:33:56,840
The Maxim's automatic firing system

654
00:33:56,841 --> 00:33:59,900
consisted of an action, a reaction, and an action.

655
00:34:00,580 --> 00:34:03,260
When a round fired, it produced a recoil force

656
00:34:03,261 --> 00:34:05,080
that loaded the next round in place.

657
00:34:05,100 --> 00:34:08,500
while simultaneously ejecting the spent cartridge.

658
00:34:08,600 --> 00:34:11,040
Maxim licensed his revolutionary new weapon

659
00:34:11,140 --> 00:34:14,840
to Great Britain and Russia, and also to Germany,

660
00:34:14,940 --> 00:34:17,740
nations soon to be enemies in World War I.

661
00:34:17,840 --> 00:34:21,040
This is the Maxim machine gun.

662
00:34:21,140 --> 00:34:24,260
This is the German model 1908.

663
00:34:24,360 --> 00:34:28,260
And this was the standard machine gun of the German army

664
00:34:28,360 --> 00:34:29,560
in World War I.

665
00:34:29,660 --> 00:34:32,000
And this large thing that people at first thought

666
00:34:32,100 --> 00:34:34,660
