681
00:35:16,460 --> 00:35:20,400
As in many wars, the technology was way ahead of the tactics.

682
00:35:20,500 --> 00:35:23,980
And generals fed the carnage by ordering their armies straight

683
00:35:24,080 --> 00:35:25,100
into the killing zone.

684
00:35:25,200 --> 00:35:29,020
The mentality of stand up and face your enemy and fight

685
00:35:29,120 --> 00:35:33,320
was still in the minds of commanders during World War I.

686
00:35:33,321 --> 00:35:36,080
No single day of the war showcased the machine guns

687
00:35:36,180 --> 00:35:40,060
lethality more than July 1, 1916,

688
00:35:40,160 --> 00:35:43,060
at the Battle of the Somme in northern France.

689
00:35:43,160 --> 00:35:46,860
Using Maxim's gun, German troops shot down wave after wave

690
00:35:46,960 --> 00:35:49,300
of attacking British infantrymen.

691
00:35:49,400 --> 00:35:54,280
By nightfall, 57,000 British troops were dead or wounded.

692
00:35:54,380 --> 00:35:57,840
It was madness to think that the infantry were still

693
00:35:57,940 --> 00:36:02,780
the prime way of carrying a position simply

694
00:36:02,781 --> 00:36:06,020
by walking into the face of machine guns.

695
00:36:06,120 --> 00:36:07,620
This devastating killing machine

696
00:36:07,720 --> 00:36:11,180
would forever change war, which is why it's number two

697
00:36:11,280 --> 00:36:12,020
on our countdown.

698
00:36:15,320 --> 00:36:17,960
Before we reveal our number one weapon,

