00:39:59,440 --> 00:40:01,840
Early derringers had another flaw.

778
00:40:01,940 --> 00:40:05,080
The gun's barrel bores were larger than its bullets.

779
00:40:05,180 --> 00:40:08,780
Pistol used to kill Lincoln had a .44 caliber gun barrel,

780
00:40:08,880 --> 00:40:11,700
but the bullet was only .41 caliber.

781
00:40:11,800 --> 00:40:14,700
This mere 3 hundredths of an inch would cause the bullet

782
00:40:14,800 --> 00:40:17,700
to bounce around inside the barrel.

783
00:40:17,800 --> 00:40:20,600
Once it left the gun, there was no telling which direction

784
00:40:20,700 --> 00:40:22,840
the bullet would fly.

785
00:40:22,841 --> 00:40:25,940
Today, every Cobra Derringer features a rifled barrel

786
00:40:26,040 --> 00:40:28,380
insert with a tighter fit.

787
00:40:28,480 --> 00:40:31,080
Once the rifling is complete, the barrel insert

788
00:40:31,180 --> 00:40:33,180
is cast into the barrel.

789
00:40:33,280 --> 00:40:35,480
Now we've got a raw Derringer barrel.

790
00:40:35,580 --> 00:40:37,280
She's going to get mated up with her frame.

791
00:40:37,380 --> 00:40:38,880
They're going to travel through the system

792
00:40:38,980 --> 00:40:40,400
and turn into a firearm.

793
00:40:40,500 --> 00:40:42,500
We're going to start at the all-important hinge hole.

794
00:40:42,600 --> 00:40:45,800
The barrel and frame are connected at the hinge hole.

795
00:40:45,900 --> 00:40:49,600
This allows the weapon to open and close for loading.

796
00:40:49,700 --> 00:40:52,840
Next, workers drill the lock hole.

797
00:40:52,841 --> 00:40:54,580
Once they put the lock in position,

798
00:40:54,680 --> 00:40:57,080
the barrel will remain fixed to the frame for firing.

799
00:40:59,980 --> 00:41:04,080
28 individually machined parts go into making every Cobra

800
00:41:04,180 --> 00:41:04,980
Derringer.

801
00:41:05,080 --> 00:41:08,480
When they're all in place, the gun is tested.

802
00:41:08,580 --> 00:41:11,800
We will test each and every gun before it leaves Cobra,

803
00:41:11,900 --> 00:41:13,900
so the end user is going to be safe.

804
00:41:14,000 --> 00:41:16,100
Weighing less than a pound and loaded

805
00:41:16,200 --> 00:41:19,940
with .22 caliber ammunition, this virgin Derringer says it

806
00:41:19,941 --> 00:41:22,440
says it all about the appeal of the handgun.

807
00:41:27,840 --> 00:41:28,940
Got him.

